<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">

  <PropertyGroup>
    <RootNamespace>MUI.Catalog</RootNamespace>
    <AssemblyName>MUI.Catalog</AssemblyName>
  </PropertyGroup>

  <!--
    The domain. Catalog must not reference MUI.Crawl: the writers that consume a probe result are not
    allowed to know a socket exists (spec §6.5), and the cheapest way to keep that true is to make the
    reference impossible.

    Persistence/ is the one place here with dependencies, and they are a database driver and a
    micro-ORM rather than another of our projects. Nothing outside Persistence/ may use them — the
    records, the interfaces and the arithmetic stay testable with no I/O at all.
  -->
  <ItemGroup>
    <PackageReference Include="Npgsql" />
    <PackageReference Include="Dapper" />
    <PackageReference Include="Microsoft.Extensions.Logging.Abstractions" />
  </ItemGroup>

  <!--
    The migrations are plain numbered .sql files at the repository root, so they can be read, diffed
    and applied by hand with psql. They are embedded here as well, so a deployed binary carries the
    schema it expects and MigrationRunner needs nothing on disk.
  -->
  <ItemGroup>
    <MigrationScript Include="$(MSBuildThisFileDirectory)..\..\migrations\*.sql" />
    <EmbeddedResource Include="@(MigrationScript)">
      <LogicalName>MUI.Catalog.Migrations.%(Filename)%(Extension)</LogicalName>
    </EmbeddedResource>
  </ItemGroup>

  <!--
    A glob that matches nothing is not an error to MSBuild, and this one lives outside the project
    directory — so a build context that did not copy migrations/ produces an assembly with an empty
    migration set, a MigrationRunner that applies nothing without complaint, and a site that starts
    against a database with no schema. Measured: the first container build here excluded migrations/
    and the image came up reading a catalogue whose tables did not exist.
  -->
  <Target Name="EnsureTheMigrationsWereFound" BeforeTargets="CoreCompile">
    <Error Condition="'@(MigrationScript)' == ''"
           Text="No .sql files were found in $(MSBuildThisFileDirectory)..\..\migrations. MUI.Catalog embeds them and MigrationRunner has nothing else to apply, so this build would produce a binary that silently applies no schema." />
  </Target>

</Project>
